WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
- I'm so happy you're here,

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.100
how have you been?

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.260
- I am good.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.500
I'm here, I could not be here,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.550
so the fact that I am

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:09.060
means that I am unbelievably well.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.150
I'm appreciative, I'm thankful,

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.110
all the above.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.980
Have nothing to complain about at all.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:15.910
Nothing.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:16.900
- All right.
Knock on some wood.

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:18.135
- I'll knock on it, too.

00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:18.968
- Knock on some wood, yes.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.820
- Obviously I know your first thought

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.660
when the accident happened,

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:23.140
was "Oh my gosh, I'm not gonna get

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.360
to see Kelly Clarkson Monday".

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.193
- That's the first thing.

00:00:25.193 --> 00:00:26.460
I know!
- The first thing.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.510
But it's okay, we're here.
- Okay, good.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.861
- I knew would care.

00:00:30.861 --> 00:00:32.210
But your pal, Dwayne Johnson,

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.650
he did us a favor though, a solid,

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.310
because y'all are really close friends,

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:36.160
and he actually came

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.510
and he represented you

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.343
on our show.

00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:40.960
- He did me a big favor, man.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.300
You know what, it was
without me even asking.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.840
He said "Kev I know you had

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:46.770
some stuff to do,

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.680
you had stuff on your plate.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:50.520
This is when you get to see

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.370
how close your brother actually is.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.203
I'm gonna stand in,

00:00:53.203 --> 00:00:54.036
and I'm gonna make sure

00:00:54.036 --> 00:00:54.950
that I can do what I can

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.700
while you're in your time of need."

00:00:57.981 --> 00:00:59.110
He's a good guy.
- He is a good guy.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:00:59.943
People don't understand

00:00:59.943 --> 00:01:01.250
the friendship is actually

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.940
100% real and authentic.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:04.870
- It looks real, yeah.

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:05.703
- For him to do the things

00:01:05.703 --> 00:01:07.131
that he did for me,

00:01:07.131 --> 00:01:08.570
it was touching.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.740
It was a heartwarming moment.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.630
I didn't tell him at the time

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:13.860
I was like, "You better do it.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.818
'Cause you don't have a choice."

00:01:15.818 --> 00:01:16.651
I said, "You don't have a choice,

00:01:16.651 --> 00:01:17.484
that's what friends go.

00:01:17.484 --> 00:01:18.840
Do it!"
- I would do it for you!

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:19.852
- No I wouldn't.

00:01:19.852 --> 00:01:21.165
I wouldn't do it for him.

00:01:21.165 --> 00:01:21.998
(laughing)

00:01:21.998 --> 00:01:23.680
- We actually have tape of him

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.513
talking about you.

00:01:24.513 --> 00:01:25.346
(air whooshing)

00:01:25.346 --> 00:01:26.179
- You hadn't actually planned

00:01:26.179 --> 00:01:27.012
on being here.

00:01:27.012 --> 00:01:28.510
Your baby brother Kevin Hart,

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:29.440
he was supposed to be here,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.520
but he was in a car accident weeks ago.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.060
So everything's good with
him now, though right?

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:32.893
He's recovering?

00:01:32.893 --> 00:01:33.726
- Everything is good,

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.559
I spoke with Kevin,

00:01:34.559 --> 00:01:35.392
and you know what,

00:01:35.392 --> 00:01:36.290
these things happen in life,

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:38.500
and thankfully he was

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.010
strapped in nicely to his car seat,

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:41.099
so I think that everything--

00:01:41.099 --> 00:01:43.440
(laughing)

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.200
- Oh my God, I love you!

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.410
- Listen, I'm only kidding.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:47.480
We spoke to the pediatrician,

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.450
and he said--

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:50.520
(laughing)

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.353
- Oh my God!

00:01:51.353 --> 00:01:52.190
- He's doing very well.

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:53.340
He's bummed he couldn't be here

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.433
as you know.

00:01:54.433 --> 00:01:55.350
(audience clapping)

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.200
- That's how I knew

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.297
y'all were real friends.
- Yeah.

